counterfactuals.output:
1. A synchronized radio-frequency (RF) ranging system comprising:

a first interrogator comprising a first RF synthesizer, a first transmitter, a first receiver, and first processing circuitry;

a second interrogator comprising a second RF synthesizer, a second receiver, and second processing circuitry; and

a synchronization interface configured to provide shared RF synthesis information to the first interrogator and the second interrogator;

wherein the first interrogator is configured to generate, using the shared RF synthesis information, a first RF interrogation signal and to transmit the first RF interrogation signal toward a target device;

wherein the target device is configured to transmit a target RF response signal in response to the first RF interrogation signal;

wherein the first receiver is configured to receive the target RF response signal at the first interrogator and to mix the received target RF response signal with a first locally generated RF signal produced using the shared RF synthesis information to generate a first mixed RF signal;

wherein the second receiver is configured to receive the target RF response signal at the second interrogator and to mix the received target RF response signal with a second locally generated RF signal produced using the shared RF synthesis information to generate a second mixed RF signal; and

wherein the first processing circuitry and the second processing circuitry are configured to determine, based at least in part on the first mixed RF signal and the second mixed RF signal, ranging information associated with the target device.
